# Optional Enterprise Answer Broker

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: Conditional governance extension
Dependencies: 27_AI_ANSWER_RESEARCH.todo, 30_AZURE_ANSWER_CONNECTION.todo

## Purpose

Add an Azure-hosted boundary only when approved governance/network requirements cannot be met by direct desktop inference.

## Tasks

- [ ] Record the concrete need: central quotas, private route, shared identity or organization-wide policy.
- [ ] Design client Entra audience/scope validation and backend managed-identity inference RBAC.
- [ ] Enforce model/endpoint/token/context allowlists and metadata-only logging.
- [ ] Preserve streaming/cancellation end-to-end; if APIM is required, disable response buffering intentionally.
- [ ] Measure hosting/cold-start/extra-hop behavior and cost against direct baseline.
- [ ] Keep no database/queue/agent/tool loop unless separately required.
- [ ] Update dependencies explicitly if this becomes the selected mandatory path; do not retrofit it silently.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Added infrastructure satisfies a documented policy requirement and measured latency budget.
- [ ] No model key or application secret is distributed to clients.
- [ ] No arbitrary upstream proxying, transcript logging or automatic region/provider fallback.
- [ ] Native desktop operation and Docker-last direction remain explicit.

## Completion evidence

- None. No broker/resource/container is created or required by the recommended baseline.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-08 - Conditional extension only; direct desktop Azure inference is the initial proposal.
